# Phase 14: Retire Legacy — P2-P3 (Delete Old Path + Complete Design)
# Status: NOT STARTED
# Depends on: Phase 11 (shadow mode proves equivalence), Phase 13 (observability confirms no regression)
# Blocks: None (final cleanup)

## Goal
Remove the legacy inline context assembly path once the pipeline has
proven stable in production. Complete remaining design aspirations.

## Why
- Dual paths (shadow mode) add complexity and maintenance burden
- Legacy code becomes dead code once pipeline is sole path
- Completing design aspirations (density tracking, adaptive placement)
  requires the pipeline to be authoritative (no fallback)

## Tasks

### 14.1 — Remove Legacy Assembly Path
- [ ] Delete inline system prompt builders that are now pipeline inputs
  - runtime/src/prompts/system.rs: build_main_system_prompt() (replaced by Bind phase)
  - runtime/src/prompts/context.rs: inline compaction logic (replaced by Optimize phase)
- [ ] Remove shadow mode infrastructure (diff logic, dual execution)
- [ ] Remove feature flag / config for shadow vs pipeline-only
- [ ] Update all call sites to use pipeline-only path
- [ ] Grep for dead code: anything importing removed functions
- [ ] Run full test suite — expect some tests to need updating

### 14.2 — Simplify Payload Construction
- [ ] chat_turn_payload.rs: remove base_payload builder (pipeline provides all fields)
- [ ] agentic_loop_turn.rs: simplify to Pipeline::run() → serialize → send
- [ ] Remove intermediate structs that existed for legacy compatibility
- [ ] Inline ContextOptimized → provider wire format (no intermediate JSON)

### 14.3 — Gateway Context Simplification
- [ ] gateway_context.rs: to_system_prompt() → becomes ContextSources.statics provider
- [ ] Remove template rendering (pipeline handles section assembly)
- [ ] Gateway passes raw context data, pipeline decides formatting
- [ ] Test: gateway integration produces identical API requests

### 14.4 — Complete Design Aspirations (Stretch)
- [ ] Information density tracking (requires LLM-as-judge per section)
  - Track which sections the model actually references in responses
  - Weight section budgets by measured utility
  - Deprioritize sections with low reference rate
- [ ] Adaptive cache breakpoint placement
  - Use N turns of cache hit data to optimize marker positions
  - A/B test marker strategies within same session
  - Converge on placement that maximizes hit ratio
- [ ] Cost-based section selection
  - User-defined section priorities (config file)
  - Budget allocation weighted by priority × information density
  - Allow user to pin/exclude specific sections

### 14.5 — Documentation & Knowledge Transfer
- [ ] Update docs/design/context-pipeline.md with final architecture
- [ ] Add operator runbook: common issues + resolution steps
- [ ] Add developer guide: how to add new section types to pipeline
- [ ] Archive Phase 1-10 commit history context in design doc

## Acceptance Criteria
- Zero dead code from legacy path remains
- Total LOC reduction >= 200 lines (removed > added)
- All tests pass with pipeline-only path
- No performance regression after legacy removal
- Design doc reflects actual shipped architecture

## Key Files (to delete or heavily modify)
- runtime/src/prompts/system.rs (legacy builder — delete most)
- runtime/src/prompts/context.rs (inline compaction — delete)
- astra-turn-core/src/chat_turn_payload.rs (simplify significantly)
- astra-cli/src/cli/chat_stream/sse_loop/agentic_loop_turn.rs (simplify)
- astra-gateway/src/gateway_context.rs (simplify to data provider)
